Subject: [PATCH] platforms: build an out-of-tree plugin dropped into src/plugins/platforms

The StarOS QPA plugin lives in its own repository and is symlinked in as
src/plugins/platforms/staros. A QPA plugin needs Qt::GuiPrivate, which is
versioned with the build and not part of the installed API, so building it
in-tree is the arrangement every platform plugin already uses.

Guarded on the directory existing, so the hunk is inert in any tree that
does not have one.

--- a/src/plugins/platforms/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -38,6 +38,9 @@
 if(QT_FEATURE_linuxfb)
     add_subdirectory(linuxfb)
 endif()
+if(EXISTS "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/staros/CMakeLists.txt")
+    add_subdirectory(staros)
+endif()
 if(QT_FEATURE_vnc AND TARGET Qt::Network)
     add_subdirectory(vnc)
 endif()
